# Fashion Image Classification using CNN

## Overview

This project implements a Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) for
classifying images from the Fashion-MNIST dataset into 10 categories.

## Technologies Used

- Python
- TensorFlow
- Keras
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
- Google Colab

## Dataset

The Fashion-MNIST dataset contains 70,000 grayscale images of clothing
items belonging to 10 different categories.

The dataset consists of:
- 60,000 training images
- 10,000 test images
- Image size: 28 × 28 pixels
- 10 classes

## Model Architecture

The CNN consists of:

- Convolutional layers
- ReLU activation
- Max Pooling layers
- Flatten layer
- Fully connected Dense layer
- Dropout
- Softmax output layer

## Methodology

1. Loaded the Fashion-MNIST dataset
2. Normalized pixel values
3. Reshaped images for CNN input
4. Built a CNN model using TensorFlow/Keras
5. Trained the model on the training dataset
6. Evaluated the model on unseen test data
7. Visualized model predictions

## Results

The model achieved a test accuracy of **89.15%**.

| Metric | Result |
|---|---:|
| Test Accuracy | 89.15% |

## How to Run

The project can be run using Google Colab or Jupyter Notebook.

Open the `.ipynb` file and execute the cells sequentially.

